# Jinja2 Safety

A helper class which sanitizes user input to prevent [Jinja2 variable 
injection](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_injection#Jinja2).

## Usage

```java
import com.google.code.jinja2.Jinja2Safety;

// The Jinja2Safety instance must be thread-safe.
Jinja2Safety safety = new Jinja2Safety();

// The render method sanitizes the input.
String html = safety.render(template, input);
```

## Example

```java
import java.io.PrintWriter;
import java.io.StringWriter;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.HashMap;
import com.google.code.jinja2.Jinja2Safety;

public class ClassX {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // The Jinja2Safety instance must be thread-safe.
        Jinja2Safety safety = new Jinja2Safety();

        // The render method sanitizes the input.
        String html = safety.render(template, input);

        // Write the sanitized output to the response.
        PrintWriter writer = new PrintWriter(System.out, true);
        writer.print(html);
    }
}
```

## Jinja2 Safety Template

The Jinja2 safety template is a [template](https://www.codecademy.com/articles/what-is-jinja)
which can be used in conjunction with the [Jinja2 template engine](http://jinja.pocoo.org/docs/2.9/)
to prevent variable injections.

The `Jinja2Safety` class uses the Jinja2 safety template to sanitize user input.

## Jinja2 Safety Template Variables

The `Jinja2Safety` template has two variables, `<|user|>` and `<|system|>`.

### <|user|>

The `<|user|>` variable is a placeholder for user input.

### <|system|>

The `<|system|>` variable is a placeholder for system input.

## Jinja2 Safety Template Usage

The Jinja2 Safety template can be used in conjunction with the Jinja2 template engine.

